  "note": "Seed replication of the 8B arm, to settle the model-scale question. The 4B-vs-8B\ndifference measured earlier (CV 7.7-16.2%, max/min 1.12-1.26) turned out to be the same size\nas this configuration's seed variance on 4B (CV 7.8-11.3%, max/min 1.19-1.27), so with one\nseed per model the two cannot be separated and the reading 'the fp8 value reached is\nmodel-dependent' had to be withdrawn.\n\nThree more seeds on 8B give that arm its own seed interval. Combined with the 4 seeds\nalready measured on 4B, the model-scale comparison becomes a comparison of two intervals\nrather than of two points, which is what deciding the question requires. A null result is\ninformative here too: overlapping intervals would mean the order-of-magnitude effect and the\nmonotonicity are all that transfers across model size, which is a cleaner practical rule\nthan a per-model multiplier.",
